---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import AppShell from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/AppShell.astro";
import Machine from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Machine.astro";
import Slider from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Slider.astro";
import Readout from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Readout.astro";
import Status from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Status.astro";
import Empty from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Empty.astro";
import Button from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Button.astro";
import Code from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Code.astro";
import Stability from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Stability.astro";
import Model from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Model.astro";
import Lost from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Lost.astro";
import ComplexStatic from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/ComplexStatic.astro";
import { u } from "../../data/nav";
---
<Docs title="Demo chrome" status="experimental" lede="The frame for an interactive figure or a small research tool: header, controls, a black stage, and a status line." wide>
  <h2>App shell</h2>
  <AppShell title="Probability machine" level={3}>
    <Fragment slot="head"><Button size="sm" variant="secondary" data-run>Run again</Button></Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="controls">
      <Slider label="Rows of pegs" name="demo-rows" min={2} max={14} value={8} hint="One more bin than rows." />
      <Slider label="Balls" name="demo-balls" min={10} max={200} step={10} value={40} />
      <Slider label="Chance of going right" name="demo-p" min={0.05} max={0.95} step={0.05} value={0.5} format="fixed2" />
    </Fragment>
    <div style="width: min(100%, 44rem); padding: 1rem"><Machine rows={8} balls={40} class="demo-machine" /></div>
    <Fragment slot="status"><Status state="idle">Ready</Status><span class="demo-counts ply-mono"></span></Fragment>
  </AppShell>
  <p>A complete version with this exact shell is the <a href={u("/patterns/demo/")}>demo page pattern</a>.</p>
  <Code lang="astro" code={`<AppShell title="Probability machine">
  <Fragment slot="head"><Button size="sm" variant="secondary">Run again</Button></Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="controls">
    <Slider label="Rows of pegs" name="rows" min={2} max={14} value={8} />
  </Fragment>
  <Machine rows={8} />                       <!-- the stage -->
  <Fragment slot="status"><Status state="idle">Ready</Status></Fragment>
</AppShell>`} />
  <p>The shell's title is an <code>h2</code>. Under a section heading of its own, pass <code>level={3}</code>, as this page does.</p>

  <h2>Readout</h2>
  <div style="max-width: 18rem"><Readout label="Run summary" items={[{ label: "Balls", value: 40 }, { label: "Mean bin", value: "4.03" }, { label: "Expected", value: "4.00" }]} /></div>
  <Code lang="astro" code={`<Readout items={[{ label: "Mean bin", value: "4.03" }]} />`} />

  <h2>Empty state</h2>
  <div style="border: 2px solid var(--ply-color-rule-strong)">
    <Empty title="No runs yet" body="Pick a dataset and press Train. Results appear here, newest first.">
      <Button size="sm">Train</Button>
    </Empty>
  </div>
  <p>An empty state says what is missing and gives the one action that fills it. Its mark is a complex with no edges yet: a few loose points. When the empty state is the page's content, as on a 404, give its title a heading level with <code>level={"{1}"}</code>, so the page has a heading.</p>

  <h2 id="model">Working model</h2>
  <p><code>Model</code> is the frame every working model on a paper page shares: a flush black panel holding one inline SVG, the controls and readout under the panel on the page ground, and an exhibit caption that says what the model is. A model illustrates a paper's mechanism, and its caption says so. The drawing's classes (<code>.ply-m-chalk</code>, <code>.ply-m-move</code>, and the rest) set chalk lines and points on the panel, mustard at half strength for filled regions, and tomato for the one moving part.</p>
  <div style="max-width: 30rem">
    <Model name="gate" title="A gate that opens at a threshold" firstRun>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 100 56" role="img" aria-label="A point on an axis. A gate stands at 60% and the region past it fills when the point crosses.">
        <line class="ply-m-rule" x1="10" y1="40" x2="90" y2="40" stroke-width="0.6" />
        <rect class="ply-m-note" data-fill x="58" y="30" width="0" height="10" />
        <line class="ply-m-chalk" x1="58" y1="22" x2="58" y2="44" stroke-width="0.8" />
        <text class="ply-m-text" x="58" y="18" font-size="4" text-anchor="middle">threshold</text>
        <circle class="ply-m-move" data-dot cx="90" cy="40" r="2.4" />
      </svg>
      <div slot="controls" class="ply-model__axis" style="--x0: 0.1; --x1: 0.9">
        <Slider label="Position" name="gate-x" value={80} />
      </div>
      <Fragment slot="caption">Drag the point past the threshold and the gate fills. On first view the point runs once from the start.</Fragment>
    </Model>
  </div>
  <Code lang="astro" code={`<Model name="gate" title="A gate that opens at a threshold" firstRun>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 100 56">...</svg>
  <div slot="controls" class="ply-model__axis" style="--x0: 0.1; --x1: 0.9">
    <Slider label="Position" name="gate-x" value={80} />
  </div>
  <Fragment slot="caption">What the model shows, and that it illustrates the mechanism.</Fragment>
</Model>`} />
  <p><code>name</code> is for the model's own script, and <code>draft</code> marks a figure not yet checked with a wall label. A slider that moves a mark along the drawing's horizontal axis wears <code>.ply-model__axis</code> with <code>--x0</code> and <code>--x1</code>, the fractions of the panel's width where the axis starts and ends, so its thumb sits under the mark at every value and width.</p>
  <p><code>firstRun</code> holds the figure back as a blank panel until the model's script draws its start state, then runs the model once, the first time it is half in view. Reduced motion skips the wait, a script that stalls shows the finished drawing after 2.5 seconds, and any input on a control ends the run. <code>js/firstrun.js</code> exports <code>firstRun(figure, {"{ duration, start, frame, end }"})</code>, which returns a player with <code>replay()</code>, and the curves <code>arrive</code>, <code>easeOut</code>, and <code>bezier</code>.</p>
  <Code lang="js" code={`import { firstRun, easeOut } from "@dario-loi/polytope/js/firstrun.js";

const player = firstRun(figure, {
  duration: 2,
  start() { setPosition(0); },
  frame(p) { setPosition(80 * easeOut(p)); },
  end(cancelled) { setPosition(80); },
});`} />

  <h2 id="lost">Page not found</h2>
  <p><code>Lost</code> sets the ways onward from an address that is not here: each a name in wood type with an arrow and a line saying what is there, hairlines between, the name turning tomato on hover. The exhibit goes beside them from 64rem and first when stacked. A complex whose radius is too small to join its points is the exhibit this was drawn for. Put it under a mast with the headline and one plain sentence, and mark the page <code>noindex</code> in <code>Seo</code>.</p>
  <div class="ply-wide ex__live" style="border: 2px solid var(--ply-color-rule-strong)">
    <Lost label="Example ways onward" ways={[
      { href: "#lost", label: "Papers", note: "Every paper, with code and BibTeX." },
      { href: "#lost", label: "Topics", note: "The same papers, grouped by subject." },
      { href: "#lost", label: "Home", note: "Who I am and what I work on." },
    ]}>
      <ComplexStatic slot="exhibit" seed={404} points={28} radius={0.12} label="A complex of unconnected points" />
    </Lost>
  </div>
  <Code lang="astro" code={`<Mast title="Page not found" lede="This page does not exist, though these ones do." compact rule />
<Lost ways={[{ href: "/papers/", label: "Papers", note: "Every paper, with code and BibTeX." }]}>
  <ComplexStatic slot="exhibit" seed={404} radius={0.12} label="A complex of unconnected points" />
</Lost>`} />
</Docs>
<script>
  import { firstRun, easeOut } from "@dario-loi/polytope/js/firstrun.js";
  // The working model's own script: a point on an axis, and the region past the threshold filling when it crosses.
  const fig = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-model="gate"]');
  const input = fig?.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("input[type=range]");
  const dot = fig?.querySelector("[data-dot]");
  const fill = fig?.querySelector("[data-fill]");
  if (fig && input && dot && fill) {
    const draw = (v: number) => {
      const x = 10 + 0.8 * v;
      dot.setAttribute("cx", String(x));
      fill.setAttribute("width", String(Math.max(0, x - 58)));
    };
    input.addEventListener("input", () => draw(Number(input.value)));
    firstRun(fig, {
      duration: 2,
      start() { input.value = "0"; draw(0); },
      frame(p) { draw(80 * easeOut(p)); },
      end() { input.value = "80"; draw(80); input.dispatchEvent(new Event("input", { bubbles: true })); },
    });
    draw(Number(input.value));
  }
</script>
<script>
  const m = document.querySelector<any>(".demo-machine");
  const status = document.querySelector(".ply-app__status .ply-status")!;
  const counts = document.querySelector(".demo-counts")!;
  const val = (n: string) => (document.querySelector(`[name="${n}"]`) as HTMLInputElement).value;
  const apply = () => {
    m.setAttribute("rows", val("demo-rows"));
    m.style.setProperty("--rows", val("demo-rows"));
    m.style.setProperty("--bins", String(Number(val("demo-rows")) + 1));
    m.setAttribute("balls", val("demo-balls"));
    m.setAttribute("p", val("demo-p"));
    run();
  };
  const run = () => { status.className = "ply-status ply-status--running"; status.textContent = "Dropping"; m.run(); };
  m.addEventListener("ply-machine-done", (e: CustomEvent) => {
    status.className = "ply-status ply-status--done"; status.textContent = "Settled";
    counts.textContent = `bins: ${e.detail.counts.join(" ")}`;
  });
  document.querySelectorAll('[name^="demo-"]').forEach((el) => el.addEventListener("change", apply));
  document.querySelector("[data-run]")!.addEventListener("click", run);
</script>
